          ],
          "content": "Proportional Reasoning–2"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.089,
            0.294,
            0.109
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.113,
            0.596,
            0.134
          ],
          "content": "1. Which of these are in inverse proportion?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.162,
            0.219,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": "(i)"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.152,
            0.748,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": "| x | 40 | 80 | 25 | 16 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| y | 20 | 10 | 32 | 50 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.265,
            0.222,
            0.283
          ],
          "content": "(ii)"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.256,
            0.749,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": "| x | 40 | 80 | 25 | 16 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| y | 20 | 10 | 12.5 | 8 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.366,
            0.225,
            0.385
          ],
          "content": "(iii)"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.357,
            0.748,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": "| x | 30 | 90 | 150 | 10 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| y | 15 | 5 | 3 | 45 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.443,
            0.744,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": "2. Fill in the empty cells if x and y are in inverse proportion."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.473,
            0.746,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "| x | 16 | 12 |  | 36 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| y | 9 |  | 48 |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.564,
            0.845,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "？ **Example 3:** 20 workers take 4 days to complete laying a road. How many days will 10 workers take to complete laying the same length of road?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.607,
            0.846,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "If we decrease the number of workers, then the number of days to complete the work will increase by the same factor. So these quantities are inversely proportional. So, $X_{1}y_{1}=X_{2}y_{2}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.675,
            0.212,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": "Thus,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.392,
            0.674,
            0.539,
            0.697
          ],
          "content": "20 \\times 4 = 10 \\times y_{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.71,
            0.564,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "y_{2} = \\frac{20 \\times 4}{10} = 8.",
          "image_source": "images/page_10_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.751,
            0.687,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "It will take 8 days for 10 workers to complete the work."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.782,
            0.847,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": "We notice that when the number of workers halved, the number of days to complete the work doubled. Quantities are inversely proportional if, when one quantity changes by a factor n, the other quantity changes by the inverse $\\frac { 1 } { n }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.875,
            0.914,
            0.912,
            0.934
          ],
          "content": "65"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
